    "body": "Coordination from #1543 (M3, issue-worker-high, branch `mkinney:issue/1543-circular-entity-law`, off upstream/main, not stacked): no `issue/1537*` branch was on the remotes yet, so the shared law is written there as ONE function the Slot can call:\n\n```rust\n// crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs, next to depth_law_of\npub(super) fn authored_law(src: &SrcRef) -> DepthLaw {\n    match src {\n        SrcRef::Entity(_) => DepthLaw::Section,\n        SrcRef::Stock | SrcRef::Selection(_) => DepthLaw::None,\n    }\n}\n```\n\n`depth_law_of` gains `OpParams::Circular { .. } => authored_law(src),` (after its `part_solid` early return, so a Stock source never reaches it). For the Slot, the suggested alignment is to keep #1522's picked arm (`Slot` with a `Selection` -> `Section`) and add `OpParams::Slot { .. } => authored_law(src),` below it; whichever PR merges second takes the other's arm in the merge. Pinned in-crate by `operation::authored_law_tests` (the law table) and in `crates/app/tests/circular_entity_law.rs`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
